I think units=FALSE makes sense if users are doing a batch analysis, while units=TRUE makes sense for users analyzing individuals interactively on the command line. I'm not sure which use case is more common, but the effort to type units=TRUE ten times on the command line is more than the effort to type units=FALSE one time in an R script.

Best,
Chris

