Hi Roy,

2) Was this 100% of the empirical variogram or the default first half zoom level / fraction? If this is 100% for the year, then I wouldn't be as concerned as if it was the default 50%. The last part of the variogram is pretty unreliable, though this then would seem to indicate that the first and last couple of locations in the timeseries are almost exactly the same, which would---to me---seem to indicate that not all of the hibernation (or other range contraction) non-stationary behavior is removed.

3) We don't have any multi-scale models running at the moment. You have to throw all of the data in and get something that is imperfect at short scales or, like you suggested, break up the data and get something that doesn't apply at the longest scales. More models are in production.

Best,
Chris

